From: fpvOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] drm: artosyn: add explicit P1 goggles panel profile

Adapt the GPL-2.0 QY45043A0 panel support from Missing-Lynk/ml-kernel
and select its stock raster and PHY independently of Ascent HDMI.
The P1 stock timing registers were checked on the connected goggles.
Keep the shared MIPI PLL pixel-clock selector: stock selector 0x200
depends on vendor initialization and gives only ~31 Hz on direct cold boot.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/artosyn/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/artosyn/Kconfig
@@ -11,3 +11,11 @@
 	  AR9311 VO controller and Artosyn DSI PHY glue. Boards must
 	  select a supported display profile and provide their output graph.
 	  Currently only ascent-1080p60 with RGB/I420 scanout is supported.
+
+config DRM_PANEL_QIYANG_QY45043A0
+	tristate "Qiyang QY45043A0 panel"
+	depends on OF && DRM && GPIOLIB
+	select DRM_MIPI_DSI
+	select DRM_PANEL
+	help
+	  Four-lane 1080p panel used by BETAFPV P1 goggles.
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/artosyn/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/artosyn/Makefile
@@ -1 +1,2 @@
